  "question": {
    "text": "Electric potential at a point 'P' due to a point charge of $5 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{C}$ is 50 V . The distance of ' P ' from the point charge is:\n(Assume, $\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}=9 \\times 10^{+9} \\mathrm{Nm}^2 \\mathrm{C}^{-2}$ )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "RdaJq",
      "text": "3 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GQweZ",
      "text": "9 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XS5nz",
      "text": "90 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4c0BJ",
      "text": "0.9 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electric potential at a point P due to a point charge, $\\left(\\because \\mathrm{K}=9 \\times 10^9\\right)$\n$V_P=\\frac{K Q}{r}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 50=\\frac{9 \\times 10^9 \\times 5 \\times 10^{-9}}{\\mathrm{r}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\mathrm{r}=\\frac{45}{50}=\\frac{9}{10}=0.9 \\mathrm{~m}=90 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
    "image": null
  },
